  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "The mass $M$ of a chemical in a system undergoing a reaction is given by the equation $M=M_0e^{-kt}$. It is known that 200 kg of the chemical reduced to 160 kg after three hours.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p13-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that there is exactly 128 kilograms of the chemical remaining after six hours.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Exactly $128\\text{ kg}$.",
          "worked": "At $t=0$, $M_0=200$. At $t=3$, $M=160$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}160&=200e^{-3k}\\\\e^{-3k}&=\\frac45\\\\-3k&=\\ln\\left(\\frac45\\right)\\\\k&=-\\frac{\\ln(4/5)}3\\\\k&=\\frac{\\ln(5/4)}3\\end{align*}$$\n\nAt $t=6$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}M(6)&=200e^{-6k}\\\\M(6)&=200e^{-2\\ln(5/4)}\\\\M(6)&=200\\left(\\frac45\\right)^2\\\\M(6)&=128\\text{ kg}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the rate at which the mass is reducing after six hours, correct to two decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Reducing at $9.52\\text{ kg/h}$; $M'(6)\\approx-9.52\\text{ kg/h}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dM}{dt}&=-kM\\\\M'(6)&=-k(128)\\\\M'(6)&=-\\frac{\\ln(5/4)}3(128)\\\\M'(6)&\\approx-9.52\\text{ kg/h}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe mass is reducing at $9.52\\text{ kg/h}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find how long it will take for 80% of the chemical to react, correct to two decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$21.64\\text{ hours}$.",
          "worked": "When 80% reacts, 20% remains: $M=0.2\\times200=40$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}40&=200e^{-kt}\\\\e^{-kt}&=\\frac15\\\\-kt&=\\ln\\left(\\frac15\\right)\\\\-kt&=-\\ln5\\\\t&=\\frac{\\ln5}{k}\\\\t&=\\frac{3\\ln5}{\\ln(5/4)}\\\\t&\\approx21.64\\text{ hours}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      }
    ]
  },
